{"availability":"available","full":"ttomohisa/htmlapps-mini-league-desk","name":"htmlapps-mini-league-desk","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"HTML","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-03T19:20:53Z","updated":"2026-10-09T09:09:53Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://ttomohisa.github.io/htmlapps-mini-league-desk/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T15:05:02.596Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T15:05:02.596Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T15:05:02.596Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T06:39:57.806Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-10T15:05:02.596Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Mini League Desk is a privacy-focused browser tool for running small round-robin events. It generates the schedule, records results and scores, shows remaining matches and standings, and keeps the active event on the device without requiring an account.","v1.0.3 pauses background page scrolling while a dialog is open. Dialog headers stay visible while their bodies scroll, keeping backup, output, result-entry, and confirmation actions reachable in short windows. Help retains its fixed header and independently scrollable reading area."],"features":["Set up a round-robin event quickly — Add 3–64 participants, optionally name the event, reorder the roster, or shuffle it.","Use the whole-event round-robin table — Switch between match list and participant × participant matrix views. Cells show ○ = win, × = loss, △ = draw, — = pending.","Keep scores as well as outcomes — In score-entry mode, the matrix keeps the result symbol and shows the row participant's score underneath, such as ○ / 3–1 and × / 1–3.","Correct mistakes without rebuilding the event — Edit or remove results, rename participants, reorder the roster, and use Undo for supported actions.","Keep and move event data locally — The active event is saved in browser storage, with JSON backup / restore for portability."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ttomohisa/htmlapps-mini-league-desk/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e9d4e823e402e861d0289edcd91409363c220fa3390e48d1ad3937cb4a143483","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T13:39:24.581Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T13:39:24.581Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Mini League Desk is a privacy-focused browser tool for running small round-robin events. It generates the schedule, records results and scores, shows remaining matches and standings, and keeps the active event on the device without requiring an account.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ttomohisa/htmlapps-mini-league-desk/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"not_required","text":"No installation or account is required.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ttomohisa/htmlapps-mini-league-desk/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"It does not provide accounts, cloud synchronization, spectator publishing URLs, or real-time multi-device collaboration.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ttomohisa/htmlapps-mini-league-desk/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"e9d4e823e402e861d0289edcd91409363c220fa3390e48d1ad3937cb4a143483","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ttomohisa/htmlapps-mini-league-desk/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T13:39:24.582Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-09T09:09:53Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ttomohisa/htmlapps-mini-league-desk/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T13:39:24.583Z","hash":"e9d4e823e402e861d0289edcd91409363c220fa3390e48d1ad3937cb4a143483","originalBytes":9262,"storedBytes":9262,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["event","league","browser","score","standings","csv","desk","json","loss","win","backup","current","mini","participant","round-robin","runtime","app","build","export","github","match","results","active","assets","data","draw","html","pages